{"name":"Delicate Ballet Blue","hex":"#c2d1e2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"delicate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily damaged or requiring careful handling.","Characterized by a fine structure or thin lines."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A delicate item of clothing, especially underwear or lingerie.","A choice dainty; a delicacy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate"},{"term":"ballet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A classical form of dance.","A theatrical presentation of such dancing, usually with music, sometimes in the form of a story."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform an action reminiscent of ballet dancing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballet"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Delicate (Taylor Swift song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Delicate\" is a song by the American singer-songwriter Taylor Swift from her sixth studio album, Reputation (2017). She wrote it with its producers, Max Martin and Shellback. An electropop and synth-pop ballad, \"Delicate\" features vocoder-manipulated vocals, dense synthesizers, and elements of tropical house and dancehall in its beats. Inspired by the events surrounding Swift's celebrity and personal life, the lyrics depict a narrator's vulnerability and anxiety over whether her blossoming romance would last."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Delicate_by_Taylor_Swift_%28Sawyr_and_Ryan_Tedder_remix%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delicate_(Taylor_Swift_song)","wikidata":"Q50413227"},{"title":"Ballet","blocks":[{"text":"Ballet is a type of performance dance that originated during the Italian Renaissance in the fifteenth century and later developed into a concert dance form in France and Russia. It has since become a widespread and highly technical form of dance with its own vocabulary. Ballet has been influential globally and has defined the foundational techniques which are used in many other dance genres and cultures. Various schools around the world have incorporated their own cultures. As a result, ballet has evolved in distinct ways."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Edgar_Degas_-_La_Classe_de_danse.jpg/330px-Edgar_Degas_-_La_Classe_de_danse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballet","wikidata":"Q41425"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Interior_of_the_Millennium_Biltm